# Example enclave config for oprf-node (placeholder hosts and values). Same
# format and rules as build/enclave/key-gen-example/forwards: both files of a
# config dir are measured into PCR2, so they hold no secrets; the Postgres
# connection string is delivered at runtime (not yet implemented).
# `environment` is passed to the node verbatim by nit, one KEY=VALUE per line,
# so it cannot carry comments or blank lines.
#
# The node needs Postgres (secret manager) and the other nodes (NODE_URLS,
# used to delegate requests over plain WebSocket); it does not talk to the
# chain. Each NODE_URLS host needs an outbound line. Those listen on
# 127.0.0.x:4321 inside the enclave, so the node binds 127.0.0.1:4321 (where
# the inbound forward delivers) instead of 0.0.0.0:4321, which would clash.
outbound db.example.internal 5432 8001
outbound node0.example.internal 4321 8002
outbound node1.example.internal 4321 8003
outbound node2.example.internal 4321 8004
inbound 4321 4321
